<title>USA: US Justice Dept allows Ingersoll acquisition.</title>
<headline>US Justice Dept allows Ingersoll acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Justice Department said Thursday it approved Ingersoll-Rand Co's acquisition of Zimmerman International Corp, a Michigan-based manufacturer of equipment used to lift and move heavy objects on assembly lines.</p>
<p>The Justice Department's antitrust division said it allowed the deal after Ingersoll-Rand agreed to end its exclusive licensing arrangement with another manufacturer, Knight Industries.</p>
<p>Zimmerman is the nation's largest manufacturer of such equipment, known as air balancers, while Knight ranks as the second largest, the department's said.</p>
</text>
